   "id": "us-tech-selloff",
   "group": "United States",
   "headline": "Wall Street's tech rout deepens after Anthropic's debut fails to settle AI nerves",
   "when": "Fri 20 Nov · US close",
   "what": "US stocks fell sharply on Friday as technology shares were sold and money moved into defensive sectors such as healthcare and staples. The dashboard's closing quote shows the S&P 500 down 3.70% at 6,910 and the Nasdaq down 5.28%. Reports I read at earlier points in the day gave smaller falls: one had the S&P 500 down 1.2% and another had the Nasdaq down 3.8%. Chipmaker shares fell close to 6%. Anthropic, newly listed, slid on its first full day of trading.",
   "why": "About 25% of your portfolio is in US stocks, mostly the two S&P 500 funds, which hold large tech names. ES-US500RMF and K-USA-A(D) are priced at their 18 Nov NAV this morning, and the S&P 500 has fallen about 5.6% since. The dashboard refreshes again at 11:30, when newer NAVs usually arrive. AAPL, META and TSLA are marked live and already show the move.",
